- Transfer a portion (or all) of the user's collateral to the liquidator (or to a liquidation reserve).  
- Use the seized collateral to cover the debt, possibly liquidating only enough collateral to bring the debt‑to‑collateral ratio back below the threshold.  
- Emit an event recording the liquidation (liquidator, user, amount seized, debt repaid).  
