DESCRIPTION: The liquidation function provides no reward or incentive to the caller (`msg.sender`). In a healthy lending market, liquidators are compensated (e.g., a liquidation bonus or a discount on seized collateral) to cover gas costs and risk. Without such incentives, rational actors have no motivation to monitor and liquidate unhealthy positions, leading to potential accumulation of bad debt and protocol insolvency over time.  
